WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.350
Well, let's get crackin'.

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:03.580
Let's-a-go.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.920
Stop messing around and start!

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.250
They bought me another cell phone!

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:35.550
Don't put it in the wash this time.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.880
I'll put it somewhere obvious.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:39.800
Hey!

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.340
Give me a hand, Tsukasa.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:42.800
Coming!

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.390
Ba.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:52.790
L.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:54.650
Sa.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.650
Mi.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:01.200
C.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.240
Huh?

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.110
There it is.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:05.450
Vinegar.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:06.330
Too much!

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.790
I'll input it for you so hand it over!

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.750
That's irritating!

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:10.750
I-It's okay.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.000
Don't worry.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.710
I can do it myself.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.150
I'm here to play!

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:17.960
Cousin Yui.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:18.920
Welcome!

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.550
Whatcha doing?

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.380
Playing a dating sim that just came out.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.180
Then I'm gonna borrow some random manga.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.560
'Kay.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:35.560
<i>This game is age restricted...</i>

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.730
<i>...but did she not notice...</i>

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.570
<i>...or is she letting it slide?</i>

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.320
<i>Which one is it, officer?</i>

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.860
And so...

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.240
...we beef things up during
Traffic Safety Awareness Week.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.660
Like detailed checks...

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.000
...and explanations of traffic laws...

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.120
It's pretty rough.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.330
And sometimes, they start yelling at you.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:55.880
<i>But when I look at how she usually acts...</i>

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.170
Scary! Scary!

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:57.590
<i>But when I look at how she usually acts...</i>

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:00.760
<i>...she's not very convincing
when talking about laws or safety!</i>

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.300
I'm totally shocked!

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.760
<i>I've heard that colds are lasting longer this year...</i>

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.830
<i>...so I need to get better quickly.</i>

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.640
<i>Based on my number...</i>

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.190
<i>...I'll probably be here a while.</i>

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.510
<i>I'll read while I wait.</i>

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.780
Mr. Ando.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.780
Mr. Shigeo Ando.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.660
Ms. Takara.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:38.250
Ms. Miyuki Takara.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.910
Are you here?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.880
Then the next person.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.020
Ms. Mariko Nishiyama.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:53.680
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.430
<i>What?!</i>

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:55.350
<i>Did they call me?!</i>

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:56.520
<i>What time is it?!</i>

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.860
<i>I need to pay more attention to my surroundings.</i>

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.650
We will soon arrive at the final stop, Kamata.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.490
<i>Where am I?!</i>

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.160
So I taught Tsukasa how to text message the other day.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.370
'Cause she had no idea after all that messing around.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.750
And she must have been really happy about it...

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.000
...since she's constantly texting me.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.720
Must suck for the recipient.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.550
Well, there's nothing to worry about.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.010
She's the type to start off excited...

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.000
...and eventually lose interest.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.640
Some people are just childish like that.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.410
She sent another one.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.070
If she doesn't get bored, you'll be pretty swamped.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.280
And does she even have that much to talk about?

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.950
We're practically together 24/7.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.450
And she apparently learned how to use symbols.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:51.910
Look.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:56.340
How about we buy soy cream-man
on the way home again today?

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.420
What's all the stuff at the end?

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.210
You can tell she's having fun...

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.210
I haven't even seen half of these before.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.220
I guess she's finally gotten the hang of it.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.420
Hey.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.960
I know how you feel...

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.620
...but could you stop spamming family members?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.710
Do you have a minute?

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:44.750
What?

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:49.130
I'm not sure about how to use
text messaging on a cell phone.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.340
<i>Hey, hey, hey!</i>

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:52.840
It's really easy, Dad.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.550
You're so hopeless.

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:56.510
I'll teach you.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.390
So I guess some people get all
snobby after they've learned something.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.350
Um...

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.730
That smell is beyond words.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.440
Right?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.690
It just stinks too much.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.950
Seriously.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.120
You've got a lot of stuff saved on here.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.240
Hey!

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.200
Stop going through that!

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.080
You've got messages that shouldn't be seen?

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.080
Not really.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.120
No reason.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.370
It's a man.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:23.960
Definitely a man.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.250
It's not!

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.770
She's not picking up.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.990
Guess I'll call her house.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.710
Hello, Kagami?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.100
Konata?

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.020
You should answer your cell.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.020
Well...

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:48.270
It didn't ring so I didn't notice.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.320
Honestly...

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.400
Doesn't that defeat the purpose?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.200
And where is that thing anyway?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:57.490
Your cell phone really serves no purpose, huh?

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:58.490
Anyway...

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:00.700
About next weekend...

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.040
Someone's talking to me.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.000
Hold on.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.710
Hey!

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:05.170
Hurry it up!

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.630
Wait a bit!

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.630
You've been on the phone too long!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:08.460
Can't wait any longer!

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:09.590
Sorry. Sorry.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.280
I got in trouble for being on the phone too long.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:13.760
Sorry.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:17.550
But I figured you guys would be lax about that stuff.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.100
Sounds like it's pretty strict.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:19.930
Nah...

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.100
We were in the middle of a fighting game.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:25.060
Tell me that earlier!

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.270
In this place...

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:33.440
...my point cards shine with an invisible magic.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.910
You end up making unplanned purchases, yeah?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.990
You really wing everything.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.580
Though I kinda understand.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.710
She's here.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.210
In this city, we have Ani**te and Ga**rs...

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:53.630
Two anime stores...

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.720
There exists a person who buys
the same thing from both stores...

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.050
Legendary Girl...

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:58.550
A!

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:05.810
Legendary Girl A shift!

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.870
Welcome!

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:26.000
The DVD for Haruhi Vol. 5's in stock!

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:27.920
Limited edition!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.040
Regular edition!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.250
All ready!

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:36.220
And we've got loads of related items!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.760
<i>That's right..</i>

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.600
<i>Just display every item we have in stock.</i>

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.720
<i>She'll buy whatever she can.</i>

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.690
I wanted a limited Aquarian Age bookmark today.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.100
Need to go to Gamers.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:51.980
No good!

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.650
Then we'll do a sleepover
this weekend and play all night.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:03.830
We usually do stuff at our place...

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.870
...but can we go to your house?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.500
I'd like to go over every now and then.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.500
It's not that you can't...

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.210
...but my dad's usually home because of work.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.470
Oh.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:22.470
So that just increases the burden on me.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:23.470
What burden?

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.810
I'm kinda looking forward to
seeing what Konata's house is like.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.400
Yo.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.150
Welcome.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:34.440
Sorry to impose.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.190
Thanks for having us today.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:37.110
Welcome.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.030
I've heard a lot about you two.

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:41.820
You're shrine maidens who live at a temple, right?

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:42.450
<i>What have you been telling him?!</i>

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.530
So do you usually wear yellow hakamas?

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.490
<i>And like, that's the first thing he has to say?</i>

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:46.870
We're here.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:49.870
This is Kona-chan's room!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:53.790
Crazy as expected.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.710
This is cute!

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.230
This door...

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:05.180
Probably hides a stash of stuff you don't want seen.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:06.600
A door that must never be opened.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:07.600
Nah.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.810
I share most of that stuff with Dad...

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.310
...so he handles storage.

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:16.940
You share...

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:17.980
Oh, yeah.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.440
Your dad's an author, right?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.910
Then have you ever gotten hooked on a
light novel or dating sim your dad wrote?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:26.330
Nah.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.320
He doesn't write any of that stuff.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.370
Really...

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.250
Didn't expect that...

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:33.830
But...

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:35.580
He likes that kind of stuff...

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.290
...so wouldn't he want to write them?

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.340
He's like a lurker...

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.090
According to him...

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:43.760
...he plays dating sims and life sims on his own time...

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:47.140
...so he doesn't feel the need
to bring it to the workplace.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:51.230
<i>I've been at a loss for words for a while now.</i>

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:52.600
<i>Guess that's the Izumi family for you.</i>

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.320
My dad was being all clingy the other day.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:02.170
So I tried saying, "You're annoying, Dad!"

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:05.030
That's a little harsh, you know.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:05.820
Then he's like...

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:09.200
Couldn't you at least say,
"I hate you, Dad!" or something?

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:09.790
No.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.500
That's not quite right either.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:17.380
But your way of thinking
wouldn't fulfill his expectations.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:17.840
Yeah.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.170
No idea what you're talking about.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.920
Let's take a break.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:27.760
This is it!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:33.270
Even TV shows are starting to look like 2ch.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.810
I guess.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:36.230
Not that I would know.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:39.060
Oh, yeah.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:43.150
For someone hardcore,
you don't use much of that lingo.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:44.780
In normal situations.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.220
In chatrooms, I'm like this.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:49.700
Wow...

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.240
Is this even Japanese?

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.750
If you can read this, you've lost.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.650
Is there anything I can help with?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.930
Then serve the salad.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:07.300
Let's eat!

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:10.680
It's great!

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:12.260
Sure is.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.720
A job well done.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:17.100
This is nothing for someone
who does housework on a daily basis.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.360
If you did more housework, you might get better.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.730
Mind your own business.

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.150
Look, Konata.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:25.340
It's perfect.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:29.640
It's a scene out of my dreams!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.330
A man eating a meal with three high school girls...

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:36.040
H-Heaven on earth...

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:36.410
Sakura...
A man eating a meal with three high school girls...

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:37.250
...happens way more than it should in dating sims.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.540
Tohsaka... Tohsaka's your sister!

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:41.710
Really now...

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.010
It gets chilly when it's late.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.430
Should have put on a jacket.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.780
A shooting star!

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.190
I couldn't make my wish three times.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:05.010
It's pretty hard when they come out of nowhere.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:09.910
But I'll pull it off one day and have my wish granted.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.120
Tsukasa's a dreamer...

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.430
But it's impossible from a practical standpoint.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.870
It's a superstition because
you know it isn't going to work.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:23.210
Why does this one have no dreams...

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:25.460
Want a drink?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.130
Thanks.

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.350
You switched hairstyles.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:30.760
For fun.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.890
While we were taking a bath.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:38.930
<i>Why do the same parts feel
so different on different people?</i>

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:40.480
A photo album.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:41.560
Can I take a look?

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:42.980
Sure.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.770
Kona-chan's so cute!

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.820
You haven't changed much.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.740
And like...

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.660
...you sure are close with your dad.

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.280
That's my mom.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:56.240
<i>No way!</i>

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:56.910
<i>So young!</i>

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.120
Don't I look like her?

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.830
<i>She was legal, right?</i>

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.050
I always wonder when I look at Dad.

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:07.500
What did Mom ever see in Dad?

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:08.630
Hey, now...

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.180
You look just like your mom, you know...

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:12.760
Then in that case...

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:15.140
What would be your type?

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.360
Mine?

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.140
When you put it that way, I don't really have any...

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.230
Really?

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:22.440
Spill it.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:26.400
Which means Mom was okay with anyone.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:29.190
And she said something about
knowing Dad since they were little.

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:31.240
Well, that's a little...

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.530
Couldn't let Dad flounder around by himself.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:35.410
You don't even hold back for your parents, huh?

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:38.410
But when I look at my mom...

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.120
In manga and games these days...

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.210
...a lot of middle schoolers look mature...

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:46.770
...and a lot of adults look really young.

00:14:48.090 --> 00:14:49.590
<i>What is this?</i>

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.800
<i>Do you want me to say something?</i>

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.970
I wish Yuki-chan could have come.

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.600
Well, she's busy.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:57.510
That's it!

00:14:57.510 --> 00:15:00.350
I'll text her so she isn't lonely.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:04.480
Miyuki's really considerate so stop that.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:06.900
I got a reply.

00:15:07.190 --> 00:15:09.070
I'm glad you're having fun.

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:13.150
I'm working hard to finish my homework right now.

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:15.260
Please invite me again next time.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.700
I forgot we had homework!

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.290
Do something, Kagami!

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:23.120
Our class didn't have any.

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:24.250
Can I go to sleep?

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:25.750
Wait!

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:28.350
That shooting star.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:32.090
It might work if I use short wishes.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:33.640
Uh, you think?

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:36.800
What are you doing?

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:40.310
Studying how to say wishes faster.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:43.560
Stop escaping reality and get your homework done.

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.020
Hey, Yuki-chan.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:51.360
I didn't get this part in class earlier.

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.150
That part?

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.610
Konata leads to Kona-chan.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:57.350
Miyuki leads to Yuki-chan.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.120
Then what nickname would you use for Kagami?

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:02.870
Kaga-chan?

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:03.790
Gami-chan?

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.330
Maybe Kyo-chan.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.750
Pronounce Kagami a different way.

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:09.920
Kyo.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:11.170
Good naming sense.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:11.210
It feels strong like her, too.
Good naming sense.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.630
It feels strong like her, too.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.090
And you could use this Kyo-chan, too

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:19.220
Th-That wasn't my intention...

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:22.600
We probably shouldn't tell Sis.

00:16:22.930 --> 00:16:25.730
Then what nickname would you give yourself?

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:26.600
Tsuka-chan?

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.740
Kasa-chan?

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.270
Hi-chan, I guess.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:32.480
It's harder with my first name.

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:33.530
I see.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:36.950
You give off the whole hi-hi image.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.160
That wasn't my intention...

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:39.780
Okay.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.150
Then I'll start calling you Hi-chan.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:44.700
What?

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.410
Huh? Huh?

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.210
But it feels kind of weird...

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.250
...if I chose it myself...

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.710
And what about that?

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:53.420
<i>That?</i>

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:55.800
Doesn't matter.

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.380
Want revenge, Sebastian?

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.130
<i>Name's Shiraishi.</i>

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:58.930
Hey!

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:02.100
Kyo-chan!

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.600
Is she calling me?

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:07.020
It's too hard to understand so stop that.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:09.140
Then how do you want me to call you?

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.940
Doesn't Kagami work?

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.730
A nickname would be better.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:15.030
Like Kona-chan or Yuki-chan...

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.110
Then call me Kagami the Great.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:22.700
Hey!

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.030
Kagami the Great!

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:26.200
She really did it!

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:27.200
What is it?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.750
Just trying it out.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.330
Sorry for the wait, Kagami the Great.

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.170
What's wrong, Kagami the Great?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.130
Whoa...

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.130
My bad...

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:37.920
Please...

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:39.630
Just call me normally.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:46.970
Good lucky!

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:48.640
Okay!

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:53.060
We're already on the booming
tenth episode of Lucky Channel!

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:55.320
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:56.780
Hello!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.860
I'm the assistant, Minoru Shiraishi!

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:00.110
And right off the bat...

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:02.610
...we have our fourth character introduction...

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.200
Kagami Hiiragi!

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:08.000
She serves as a punch line character in the show.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.500
But isn't she just a tsundere?

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:13.500
What an obvious setup.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:14.540
I beg to differ.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:20.260
The classification of Kagami Hiiragi
as a tsundere is a bit hasty.

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.470
Then what?

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:26.720
First, do we comprehend the true
meaning of the qualities of a tsundere?

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.060
No, unfortunately...

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:30.890
...the word tsundere has suffered misuse and decay...

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:33.980
...and one could say that the definition has evolved.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:37.150
To begin with, the word tsundere
was born in the year 2002...

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:38.690
...an Internet term...

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.690
...but the original definition was...

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:41.860
...a character who starts off hostile...

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.280
...and eventually becomes affectionate.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.030
Yes!

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:44.530
In other words...

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.870
...it was supposed to describe a change over time!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:48.810
Do you really understand?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:49.830
And now...

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:52.790
...it is used to describe the
multiple faces of a character.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:53.370
In other words...

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:54.670
...hostile on the outside...

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:55.880
...and affectionate on the inside...

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:58.170
...would be how the word is currently understood.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.260
I declare here!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.970
This is plainly a mistake!

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:05.760
We must bring back the true meaning of tsundere...

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.470
...and restore this depraved nation!

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:10.270
Rise up, citizens!

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.560
Not bad, Sebastian.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.350
Who's that?

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:16.860
So what is Kagami if not a tsundere?

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:17.650
You meant me?

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:20.860
I don't really get this complicated stuff...

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.780
...but if you insist...

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:26.030
...do you have a replacement for
what's currently known as tsundere?

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.200
Uh...

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.330
It's not that I don't...

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.580
Maybe cool-dere...

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.040
No, that's wrong.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:32.750
Deretsun?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.460
You got no sense at all.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.250
Tsundere's fine.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.590
No, that's...

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.420
That's wrong!

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:42.340
That's it!

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:46.340
Let's ask the viewers to
come up with a new expression!

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:47.220
Good idea!

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:48.470
Delegating, huh?

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:50.470
So, everyone in front of the TV!

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:51.970
Yes, you!

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:55.560
Try to come up with a new word
to describe characters like Kagami!

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:58.770
And rewrite the modern lexicon!

00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:00.900
Dubbed the Complete Tsundere Debate!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.690
You can find more details
on the radio show and home page!

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:06.730
We're waiting for your passionate ideas!

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.540
This is the end.

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:12.240
Oh, well.

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:16.170
Lots and lots...

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:17.820
Bye-bee.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:19.630
Bye-bee!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.750
Fast forward!

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:24.920
Whoa, I talked a lot today.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.890
The most ever, yeah?

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:28.840
Huh?

00:20:28.840 --> 00:20:29.720
Akira-sama?

00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:31.890
Wh-What's wrong?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.020
Satisfied?

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.140
Yes! Uh...

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:35.890
This is the most I've ever spoken.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:37.380
I think I did a fair job.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:42.460
I'm going to dinner with the
executive and producer from your studio.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:44.330
Uh...

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:47.460
We're gonna discuss your future.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:48.980
Uh, h-hold on a sec.

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:50.540
What do you mean?

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:56.040
No point in telling you about
how your future's looking.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:56.750
No, no, no, no, no!

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:59.790
And aren't you still working at CoCo*chi?

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.250
That's only during the day.

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:03.090
And it doesn't pay much.

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:04.210
And the grill place?

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:05.550
I'm still doing that.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.170
Or that doesn't even matter!

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:09.010
That's intruding into my privacy so stop!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.390
I'm next.

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:16.270
Tsukasa.

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:17.770
How about this one?

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.190
This works!

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.190
Right, Yuki-chan?

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:21.400
I know this.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.150
Then sing it.

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:24.480
Thanks, Kona-chan.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:25.780
Thank you very much.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:26.780
No problem.

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.280
They chose a song?

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:37.620
This song was popular when
we were in preschool, right?

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.790
Don't really know.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:39.710
I'm sorry.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.960
Neither do I.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:42.170
I remember.

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:44.460
Our older sisters sang it a lot.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.420
Songs sung by parents and older siblings...

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.300
...while from an earlier generation...

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:52.050
...tend to be memorable.

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:23.960
Caved, huh?

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:25.380
Can't be helped.

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:26.690
It's really high.

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:43.520
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:22:43.520 --> 00:22:44.520
I'm Kagami.

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:46.940
When you go out to eat...

00:22:46.940 --> 00:22:49.230
...and order something with liquids...

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:51.990
...and a few drops splatter onto your clothes...

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:53.490
...it's pretty depressing.

00:22:53.490 --> 00:22:56.410
And it really sucks if it's curry sauce.

00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:59.240
And you happen to be wearing your favorite clothes.

00:22:59.240 --> 00:23:02.620
Leaves you down the whole day!

00:23:02.620 --> 00:23:05.830
And when you buy a box lunch
with sauce from a convenience store...

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:09.670
...and you carry it level so the contents don't spill...

00:23:09.670 --> 00:23:11.170
...but once you open the bag...

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:14.380
...you discover that it spilled
inside and everything's a mess.

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:16.800
Makes you lose your appetite.

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:21.020
And when you ask them to bag
hot items and cold items separately...

00:23:21.020 --> 00:23:25.060
...and they bag the cold drinks with your magazines...

00:23:25.060 --> 00:23:27.650
...and the paper sucks up the condensation...

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:29.570
...and the magazine's all soggy...

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:32.920
...and you're like what was the
point in bagging them separately then?!

00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:34.150
Next time:

00:23:34.150 --> 00:23:36.280
The Many Ways to Spend Christmas Eve.

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:37.730
Look forward to next time!
